<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teraupoʻo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1880s–1897</span> · Also known as Teraupo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teraupoʻo was a chief of Raiatea in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a> who led armed resistance against French annexation of the island, proclaimed in 1888. His followers held out in the interior for nearly a decade, until a French expedition put down the rising and captured him in 1897, bringing Raiatea under full French control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teraupoo.jpg" alt="Teraupoʻo" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jules Agostini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raiatea_-_Le_Chef_Teraupoo_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
